        <h1> Craig Innes </h1>

        <h2>Introduction / Motivation</h2> 

        <p> I am a Chancellor's Fellow within the <a href="https://web.inf.ed.ac.uk/ipab"> Institute for Perception, Action and Behaviour (IPAB) </a> at the University of Edinburgh. I'm interested in guarantees on safety, trustworthiness and risk for cyber-physical systems. In particular - how can we combine traditional models of symbolic-logic and formal verification, with newer black-box probabilistic models seen in modern complex machine learning systems? </p>

        <p> Previously, I worked as a postdoctoral researcher in the <a href="https://rad.inf.ed.ac.uk/">UoE Robust Autonomy and Decisions Group (RAD)</a>. Before that, I did a Phd in the <a href="http://web.inf.ed.ac.uk/ilcc">Institute for Language, Cognition and Computation (ILCC)</a>, which was all about the semantics of unawarness (or "unknown unknowns"). Its still available <a href="https://era.ed.ac.uk/bitstream/handle/1842/36129/Innes2019.pdf">here</a> if you're interested.</p> 

        <p>In my spare time I used to design small video games. You can find a list of them on my <a href="https://craiginnes.itch.io/"> Itch.io </a> page. If you're interested in making games, I suggest using <a href="https://godotengine.org/">Godot</a> then joining a <a href="http://www.ludumdare.com">Game Jam </a> to get inspired. </p>

        <h3 class="red-announce"> PhD Positions at University of Edinburgh </h3>
        <p> I'm currently open to new PhD students (home or international) at the University of Edinburgh. I am particularly interested in supervising students around the topics of <b> Safety & Trustworthiness for AI and Cyber-Physical Systems (Robots and Autonomous Vehicles) </b>. The best ways to apply are through:
        
        <ul>
          <li> As part of the Centre for Doctoral Training on <a href="https://www.edinburgh-robotics.org/apply"> Dependable and Deployable Robotics </a> </li>
          <li> As part of the Centre for Doctoral Training on <a href="https://mlsystems.uk/"> ML Systems </a></li>
          <li> Directly via the <a href="https://postgraduate.degrees.ed.ac.uk/?r=site/view&id=495"> Institute for Perception, Action, and Behaviour</a></li>
        </ul> 
          
        <p> I also wrote a short <a href="blog/posts/2023-10-25-PhD-Application-Guide"> FAQ for applying to study a PhD at Edinburgh </a>. Feel free to email me if you have any further questions. </p>

